  <h2>Is AloSIM or Ubigi the Right Pick</h2>
  <div class="decision-grid">
    <div class="decision-card decision-card--primary">
      <h3>Go with AloSIM if&hellip;</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>You want a temporary international number for verification texts or booking calls</li>
        <li>You want to buy ahead and keep a refund option until you activate</li>
        <li>You want a single one-off purchase with no recurring commitment</li>
        <li>You want the larger code (15%)</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="decision-card decision-card--secondary">
      <h3>Go with Ubigi if&hellip;</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>You visit the same country on a schedule and a monthly plan beats buying a new eSIM each time</li>
        <li>You prefer an established carrier-side company over a smaller reseller</li>
        <li>You are fine with a 3-month minimum on a monthly plan or a non-refundable annual term</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Two Things Worth Knowing Before You Decide</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Read the plan type on Ubigi before paying.</strong> A recurring plan looks like any other purchase at checkout but carries a lock-in. If you only want one trip, make sure you picked a one-off plan.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>AloSIM's refund window is about activation.</strong> The guarantee covers eSIMs that fail to connect, not ones you activated and used. Wanting unlimited data with no meter? <a href="/holafly/">Holafly</a> is built around that. For device setup, see our <a href="/compatible-devices/">eSIM compatible devices</a> guide.
  </p>

  <h2>AloSIM vs Ubigi FAQ</h2>
  <div class="content-faq">
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Which is cheaper, AloSIM or Ubigi</h3>
      <p>It depends on the destination, so check both at checkout. AloSIM's code is 15% against Ubigi's 10%, but Ubigi's per-GB price tends to sit above most providers on this site.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Does either include a phone number</h3>
      <p>AloSIM offers a free international number through Hushed, set up in the AloSIM app after purchase. We haven't seen an equivalent on Ubigi.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Can I cancel a Ubigi plan</h3>
      <p>One-off plans are a single purchase. A monthly recurring plan can't be cancelled for the first three months, and an annual plan can't be cancelled or refunded during the year.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Does an unused plan expire</h3>
      <p>An unused AloSIM plan doesn't expire. Check the plan details on Ubigi before buying ahead.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

